Luthier @LUTHIER_VERSION@ for Linux (x86-64)
=====================================

Contents of this folder

  Luthier                 standalone application
  Luthier.vst3/           VST3 plugin (absent from the "-standalone" bundle)
  Resources/              factory content: impulse responses, parts, guitars,
                          tunes, fonts. Both binaries look for it beside
                          themselves; Luthier.vst3/Resources links to it.
  install.sh              copies the above into place (user or system)
  uninstall.sh            removes exactly what install.sh wrote
  luthier.desktop, luthier.xml, icons/   desktop entry, file types, icons
  THIRD_PARTY_LICENCES.txt

Run in place ("portable")

  ./Luthier               runs from this folder; nothing is installed.
                          Your presets, guitars and settings still live in
                          ~/Documents/Luthier and ~/.config (see the manual).
  A DAW can be pointed at this folder's Luthier.vst3 directly.

Install

  ./install.sh --user     ~/.vst3, ~/.local/bin, ~/.local/share/luthier
  sudo ./install.sh --system
                          /usr/lib/vst3, /usr/bin, /opt/Luthier
  ./install.sh --help     the options

Uninstall

  ./uninstall.sh          (or: ~/.local/share/luthier/uninstall.sh,
                           /opt/Luthier/uninstall.sh)
  ./uninstall.sh --purge  also deletes your presets, guitars and settings

Requirements

  ALSA (libasound2), X11, freetype and fontconfig. JACK or PipeWire-JACK
  are used when present. The .deb lists the exact packages.

Full instructions: docs/INSTALL_LINUX.md in the source tree.
